  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Information :</strong></span> has released the Exam City Details for the post of Junior Hindi Translator (JHT)/ Junior Translation Officer (JTO)/ Junior Translator (JT), Junior Translation Officer (JTO) &amp; Senior Hindi Translator (SHT)/Senior Translator (ST)/ Senior Translation Officer (STO) on the official website. This recruitment has been issued for 303 posts. The online application process for SSC JHT Recruitment 2026 were accepted from 23 April 2026, to 14 May 2026. The Examination is going to conducted on 08 September 2026. Candidates must check the complete details for SSC JHT Exam Date 2026, which are given below.</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Staff Selection Commission (SSC)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">SSC JHT Exam City Details 2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Application Start Date : <strong>23 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Last Date : <span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>14 May 2026</strong></span></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Fee Payment Last Date : <strong>15 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Form Correction Date : <strong>19-20 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\">Exam Date : <strong>08 September 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Exam City Details : <strong>31 August 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Admit Card :<strong> Before Exam</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General, EWS, OBC :<strong> Rs. 100/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC, ST :<strong> Rs. 0/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">All Category Female :<strong> Rs. 0/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[adinserter block=”3″]</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>SSC JHT Notification 2026 : Age Limit</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Age Limit As On 01 August 2026</span></strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Minimum Age :&nbsp;<strong>18 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>30 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per SSC JHT Recruitment Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>SSC JHT 2026 : Vacancy Details</strong></span></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Total Posts : 303</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.2924%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.5584%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Category&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.1491%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>No. of Post&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.2924%; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"5\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Junior Hindi Translator (JHT) &amp; Senior Hindi Translator (SHT)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.5584%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.1491%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.5584%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">EWS</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.1491%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.5584%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">OBC</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.1491%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.5584%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.1491%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.5584%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">ST</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.1491%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>SSC JHT Recruitment 2026 : Educational Qualification</b></span></h3>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.8554%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.1446%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.8554%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Junior Hindi Translator (JTO) in Central Secretariat Official Language Servise (CSOLS)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.1446%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates having&nbsp;&nbsp;Master Degree in Hindi or English with English or Hindi as a Compulsory Subjects <strong>OR</strong> Master Degree in Any Subject with English Medium and Hindi as a Compulsory Subject in Degree Level And Recognized Diploma Course in Translation from Hindi to English Vice Versa or 2 Year Experience will be eligible for this post.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.8554%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Junior Translation Officer (JTO) in Armed Forces Headquarters (AFHQ)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.1446%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates having&nbsp;&nbsp;Master Degree in Hindi or English with English or Hindi as a Compulsory Subjects <strong>OR</strong> Master Degree in Any Subject with English Medium and Hindi as a Compulsory Subject in Degree Level And Recognized Diploma Course in Translation from Hindi to English Vice Versa or 2 Year Experience will be eligible for this post.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.8554%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Junior Hindi Translator (JHT)/ Junior Translation Officer(JTO)/Junior Translator (JT) in various Central Government Ministries/ Departments/ Organizations</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.1446%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates having&nbsp;&nbsp;Master Degree in Hindi or English with English or Hindi as a Compulsory Subjects <strong>OR</strong> Master Degree in Any Subject with English Medium and Hindi as a Compulsory Subject in Degree Level And Recognized Diploma Course in Translation from Hindi to English Vice Versa or 2 Year Experience will be eligible for this post.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.8554%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Senior Hindi Translator (SHT)/Senior Translator (ST) in various Central Government Ministries/ Departments/ Organizations</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.1446%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Master Degree in Hindi or English with English or Hindi as a Compulsory Subjects OR Master Degree in Any Subject with English Medium and Hindi as a Compulsory Subject in Degree Level And Recognized Diploma Course in Translation from Hindi to English Vice Verca or 3 Year Experience&nbsp;will be eligible for this post.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>SSC JHT Exam City Details 2026 : How To Download</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Check the Important Links section.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Then click on the Download Exam City Details link.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">After clicking on the link, candidates will be redirected to the Dashboard page.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">In this page candidates have to fill up the following fields with proper details:</span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Candidate’s Registration Number</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Date of Birth</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Gender</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Verification Code</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Then the candidates will be required to submit the details in order to download the Exam City Details.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">The candidate can also download their Exam City Details download from the official Website.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>SSC JHT Recruitment 2026 : Mode of Selection</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Paper-I Written Exam</span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Paper-II Written Exam</span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Medical Examination</span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Document Verification</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[adinserter block=”3″]</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable2\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"t